===Mergers===
*On [[June 1]], [[1993]], the town of [[Kamisato, Nagano|Kamisato]] from [[Shimoina District, Nagano|Shimoina District]] merged into the expanded city of [[Iida, Nagano|Iida]].

*On [[September 1]], [[2003]], the city of [[Koshoku, Nagano|Koshoku]], the town of [[Kamiyamada, Nagano|Kamiyamada]] from [[Sarashina District, Nagano|Sarashina District]] and the town of [[Togura, Nagano|Togura]] from [[Hanishina District, Nagano|Hanishina District]] merged into the city of [[Chikuma, Nagano|Chikuma]].

*On [[April 1]], [[2004]], the village of [[Kitamimaki, Nagano|Kitamimaki]] from [[Kitasaku District, Nagano|Kitasaku District]] and the town of [[Tobu, Nagano|Tobu]] from [[Chiisagata District, Nagano|Chiisagata District]] merged to form the new city of [[Tomi, Nagano|Tomi]].

*On [[January 1]], [[2005]], the village of [[Ooka, Nagano|Ooka]] from [[Sarashina District, Nagano|Sarashina District]], the town of [[Toyono, Nagano|Toyono]] and the villages of [[Togakushi, Nagano|Togakushi]] and [[Kinasa, Nagano|Kinasa]] (all three from [[Kamiminochi District, Nagano|Kamiminochi District]]) merged into the city of [[Nagano, Nagano|Nagano]]. [[Sarashina District, Nagano|Sarashina District]] was dissolved as a result.

*On [[February 13]], [[2005]], the village of [[Yamaguchi, Nagano|Yamaguchi]] from [[Kiso District, Nagano|Kiso District]] merged into the city of [[Nakatsugawa, Gifu|Nakatsugawa]] in [[Gifu Prefecture]].

*On [[March 20]], [[2005]], the town of [[Saku, Nagano (Minamisaku)|Saku]] and the village of [[Yachiho, Nagano|Yachiho]] from [[Minamisaku District, Nagano|Minamisaku District]] merged to form the new town of [[Sakuho, Nagano|Sakuho]].

*On [[April 1]], [[2005]], the town of [[Usuda, Nagano|Usuda]] from [[Minamisaku District, Nagano|Minamisaku District]], and the town of [[Mochizuki, Nagano|Mochizuki]] and the village of [[Asashina, Nagano|Asashina]] (both from [[Kitasaku District, Nagano|Kitasaku District]]) merged into the city of [[Saku, Nagano|Saku]].

*On [[April 1]], [[2005]], the village of [[Narakawa, Nagano|Narakawa]] from [[Kiso District, Nagano|Kiso District]] merged into the city of [[Shiojiri, Nagano|Shiojiri]].

*On [[April 1]], [[2005]], the village of [[Toyota, Nagano|Toyota]] from [[Shimominochi District, Nagano|Shimominochi District]] merged into the city of [[Nakano, Nagano|Nakano]].

*On [[April 1]], [[2005]], the village of [[Shiga, Nagano|Shiga]] from [[Higashichikuma District, Nagano|Higashichikuma District]], and the villages of [[Nagawa (Minamiazumi), Nagano|Nagawa]], [[Azumi, Nagano|Azumi]] and [[Azusagawa, Nagano|Azusagawa]] from [[Minamiazumi District, Nagano|Minamiazumi District]] merged into the city of [[Matsumoto, Nagano|Matsumoto]].

*On [[October 1]], [[2005]], the villages of [[Mure, Nagano|Mure]] and [[Samizu, Nagano|Samizu]] from [[Kamiminochi District, Nagano|Kamiminochi District]] merged to form the new town of [[Iizuna, Nagano|Iizuna]].

*On [[October 1]], [[2005]], the town of [[Akashina, Nagano|Akashina]] from [[Higashichikuma District, Nagano|Higashichikuma District]], and the towns and villages of [[Horigane, Nagano|Horigane]], [[Hotaka, Nagano|Hotaka]], [[Misato, Nagano|Misato]] and [[Toyoshina, Nagano|Toyoshina]] from [[Minamiazumi District, Nagano|Minamiazumi District]] merged to form the new city of [[Azumino, Nagano|Azumino]]. [[Minamiazumi District, Nagano|Minamiazumi District]] was dissolved as a result.

*On [[October 1]], [[2005]], the villages of [[Kami, Nagano|Kami]] and [[Minamishinano, Nagano|Minamishinano]] from [[Shimoina District, Nagano|Shimoina District]] merged into the city of [[Iida, Nagano|Iida]].

*On [[October 1]], [[2005]], the town of [[Nagato, Nagano|Nagato]] and the village of [[Wada, Nagano|Wada]] from [[Chiisagata District, Nagano|Chiisagata District]] merged to form the new town of [[Nagawa, Nagano|Nagawa]].

*On [[October 11]], [[2005]], the villages of [[Honjo, Nagano|Honjo]], [[Sakakita, Nagano|Sakakita]] and [[Sakai, Nagano|Sakai]] from [[Higashichikuma District, Nagano|Higashichikuma District]] merged to form the new village of [[Chikuho, Nagano|Chikuho]].

*On [[November 1]], [[2005]], the villages of [[Kisofukushima, Nagano|Kisofukushima]], [[Mitake, Nagano|Mitake]], [[Hiyoshi, Nagano|Hiyoshi]] and [[Kaida, Nagano|Kaida]] from [[Kiso District, Nagano|Kiso District]] merged to form the new town of [[Kiso Town, Nagano|Kiso]].

*On [[January 1]], [[2006]], the villages of [[Yasaka, Nagano|Yasaka]] and [[Miasa, Nagano|Miasa]] from [[Kitaazumi District, Nagano|Kitaazumi District]] merged into the city of [[Omachi, Nagano|Omachi]].

*On [[January 1]], [[2006]], the village of [[Namiai, Nagano|Namiai]] from [[Shimoina District, Nagano|Shimoina District]] merged into the village of [[Achi, Nagano|Achi]].

==Demographics==

==Culture==

==Tourism==
===Tourist spots===
*[[Matsumoto Castle]], one of Japan's national treasures.
*One of the world's highest [[geyser]]s (about 40 to 50 meters) in [[Suwa]].

==Prefectural symbols==

==Miscellaneous topics==

* Nagano's current governor, [[Yasuo Tanaka]], is an independent who has made a reputation internationally for attacking Japan's status quo. Among other issues, he has refused national government money for construction projects that he deems unnecessary, such as dams, and has overhauled (locally) the press club system that is blamed for limiting government access to journalists who give favorable coverage.

